-- title:
--   Refinement of a subdivided multigraph: Laplacian rows under extension by zero
-- statement:
--   Fix $n,m\in\mathbb{N}$, maps $\mathrm{src},\mathrm{tgt}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathrm{Fin}\,n$, weights $W:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathbb{N}$ with $W_e>0$ for all $e$, an integer $M>0$, and weights $W'$ with $W'_e = M\,W_e$ for all $e$. Let $V=\mathrm{Fin}\,n\sqcup\coprod_e\mathrm{Fin}(W_e-1)$, and for a pair $\varepsilon=(e,k)$ with $k<W_e$ let $\mathrm{ends}(\varepsilon)$ be the pair whose first entry is $\mathrm{src}(e)$ if $k=0$ and the interior vertex $(e,k-1)$ otherwise, and whose second entry is $\mathrm{tgt}(e)$ if $k+1=W_e$ and the interior vertex $(e,k)$ otherwise; thus the segments $\varepsilon$ subdivide edge $e$ into $W_e$ pieces. Put $\mathrm{lap}(v)=\sum_\varepsilon\bigl([\mathrm{ends}(\varepsilon)_1=v](\delta_v-\delta_{\mathrm{ends}(\varepsilon)_2})+[\mathrm{ends}(\varepsilon)_2=v](\delta_v-\delta_{\mathrm{ends}(\varepsilon)_1})\bigr)\in\mathbb{Z}^V$, where $\delta$ denotes `Pi.single`, and let $V'$, $\mathrm{ends}'$, $\mathrm{lap}'$ be the same data built from $W'$. Let $\iota:V\to V'$ be the identity on $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ and send the interior vertex $(e,j)$ to $(e,M(j+1)-1)$, and let $\rho:\mathbb{Z}^V\to\mathbb{Z}^{V'}$ be the additive map whose $v'$-th coordinate is the sum of the coordinates over the fibre $\iota^{-1}(v')$. The conclusion asserts seven statements: $\iota$ is injective; $\rho x(v')$ equals that fibre sum; $\rho x(\iota v)=x(v)$; $\rho x(v')=0$ for $v'$ outside the image of $\iota$; $\rho(\delta_v c)=\delta_{\iota v}c$ for all $v$ and $c\in\mathbb{Z}$; $\rho(\mathrm{lap}(u))$ lies in the subgroup of $\mathbb{Z}^{V'}$ generated by the range of $\mathrm{lap}'$, for every $u\in V$; and consequently the subgroup generated by the range of $\mathrm{lap}$ is contained in the preimage under $\rho$ of the subgroup generated by the range of $\mathrm{lap}'$.
--
--   This is the combinatorial compatibility, under $M$-fold refinement of a subdivided multigraph, between the lattices spanned by the Laplacian rows (the lattices whose quotients are the Jacobians of the two graphs): extension by zero along the inclusion of coarse vertices carries coarse Laplacian rows into the fine Laplacian lattice. It is used in the analysis of component groups attached to a semistable covering, in the proof of [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_pow_zsmul_mk_eq_zero_forall_mu_sub_eq_sum_smul_lap_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_pow_zsmul_mk_eq_zero_forall_mu_sub_eq_sum_smul_lap_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel).
